# Repo-only files, excluded from the published pub package.
#
# A `.pubignore` REPLACES the `.gitignore` in its directory as far as pub is
# concerned — pub reads one or the other, never both — so everything the root
# `.gitignore` keeps out of git must be listed here again, or `dart pub
# publish` ships it (a stray `flutter_01.log`, a local `coverage/`). Hidden
# files and directories (`.dart_tool/`, `.github/`, `.demos/`, `.DS_Store`)
# are always left out by pub itself, and `example/.gitignore` still applies
# inside `example/`.
#
# `screenshots/` stays in the archive — pub.dev renders the images the
# pubspec's `screenshots:` section points at, so they must ship with the package.
# `shaders/` must stay in the archive too: `beam.frag` is declared under
# `flutter: shaders:` and compiled into every consuming app. Never ignore it.

# ── Mirrors of the root .gitignore ──────────────────────────────────────────
*.class
*.log
*.pyc
*.swp
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
migrate_working_dir/
**/doc/api/
**/build/
coverage/

# ── Repo-only sources and tooling ───────────────────────────────────────────
assets/
tool/
CLAUDE.md
# codecov.yml, plus the uploader binary and its checksums that
# codecov/codecov-action downloads into the working tree in CI.
/codecov*
# Golden reference images only matter to the repo's own CI, not to consumers.
test/**/golden/
